From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:10:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] leds: flash: qcom: Release every V4L2 flash device
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The array of V4L2 flash devices holds leds_count entries, from 0 to
leds_count - 1, but removal and the probe's error path walk it from
index leds_count down to 1. Removal reads one entry past the end of the
array, and neither ever releases the first device; the error path also
stops at once, as the entry of the LED that failed is still empty.
Release entries leds_count - 1 down to 0 instead.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c b/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
index e5820091d..416902454 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
@@ -956,8 +956,8 @@ static int qcom_flash_led_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	return regmap_field_write(flash_data->r_fields[REG_TORCH_CLAMP], flash_data->torch_clamp);
 release:
-	while (flash_data->v4l2_flash[flash_data->leds_count] && flash_data->leds_count)
-		v4l2_flash_release(flash_data->v4l2_flash[flash_data->leds_count--]);
+	while (flash_data->leds_count)
+		v4l2_flash_release(flash_data->v4l2_flash[--flash_data->leds_count]);
 	return rc;
 }
 
@@ -965,8 +965,8 @@ static void qcom_flash_led_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct qcom_flash_data *flash_data = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
-	while (flash_data->v4l2_flash[flash_data->leds_count] && flash_data->leds_count)
-		v4l2_flash_release(flash_data->v4l2_flash[flash_data->leds_count--]);
+	while (flash_data->leds_count)
+		v4l2_flash_release(flash_data->v4l2_flash[--flash_data->leds_count]);
 
 	mutex_destroy(&flash_data->lock);
 }
